{"qid": "2wikimqa:37022dee1597491021c2aa7522276a600eb0dd316f12cbb6", "question": "Who is the paternal grandmother of Marie Of Brabant, Queen Of France?", "answers": ["Marie of Hohenstaufen"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\nMarie of Brabant, Queen of France (1254–1322) was the daughter of **Henry III, Duke of Brabant** and Adelaide of Burgundy [1]. Therefore, her paternal grandmother is the mother of Henry III, Duke of Brabant.\n\nFrom the historical record, Henry III, Duke of Brabant was the son of **Henry II, Duke of Brabant** and **Maria of Swabia (Marie of Hohenstaufen)**. So the paternal grandmother of Marie of Brabant, Queen of France was **Maria of Swabia**.\n\nNote: the knowledge base explicitly confirms her father was Henry III, Duke of Brabant [1] and that he descended through the Brabant ducal line [3], but the retrieved snippets did not directly name Henry III's own mother — that final step comes from standard genealogical records rather than the retrieved chunks.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 105385.7, "error": ""}
