{"qid": "2wikimqa:40de6f6c353c080845a8ea644039e9ba83cd481d3745395b", "question": "Who is Archibald Acheson, 4Th Earl Of Gosford's paternal grandfather?", "answers": ["Archibald Acheson, 2nd Earl of Gosford"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Archibald Acheson, 2nd Earl of Gosford** was the paternal grandfather of Archibald Acheson, 4th Earl of Gosford.\n\nReasoning chain from the retrieved evidence:\n\n1. The 4th Earl, Archibald Brabazon Sparrow Acheson (1841–1922), was the son of Archibald Acheson, 3rd Earl of Gosford[2].\n2. The 3rd Earl (born 20 August 1806) \"was the only son of Archibald Acheson, 2nd Earl of Gosford\" and Mary Sparrow[3].\n\nTherefore, going two generations up the male line from the 4th Earl: 4th Earl → father (3rd Earl) → paternal grandfather (**Archibald Acheson, 2nd Earl of Gosford**).\n\n(Note: Arthur Acheson, 1st Earl of Gosford, mentioned in the evidence, would be the 4th Earl's *great*-grandfather, not his grandfather.)", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 163327.0, "error": ""}
