{"qid": "2wikimqa:57543e0892f90733bf97dc270cdb36eb9bf8e2230940bcb9", "question": "Which film has the director who died first, Tex And The Lord Of The Deep or Henry Goes Arizona?", "answers": ["Henry Goes Arizona"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Henry Goes Arizona** has the director who died first.\n\n- **Henry Goes Arizona** (1939) was directed by **Edwin L. Marin**, who lived from February 21, 1899 to **May 2, 1951**[7][10].\n- **Tex and the Lord of the Deep** (1985) was directed by **Duccio Tessari**[1][3]. Since Tessari directed and released this film in 1985, he was still alive decades after Marin's death, meaning his death necessarily came later.\n\nTherefore, Edwin L. Marin (director of *Henry Goes Arizona*) died first, in 1951.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 103513.0, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:5ff6349ea0b2ecb882f535ff3cec2f9c012d3468fb7b912e", "question": "Who is the mother-in-law of Louise Of Mecklenburg-Güstrow?", "answers": ["Charlotte Amalie of Hesse-Kassel"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, the knowledge base confirms Louise of Mecklenburg-Güstrow was born at Güstrow as the daughter of Duke Gustav Adolph of Mecklenburg-Güstrow and Duchess Magdalena Sibylla of Holstein-Gottorp[4], and she became Crown Princess of Denmark[5].\n\nLouise married the future King Frederick IV of Denmark. Therefore, her mother-in-law was **Charlotte Amalie of Hesse-Kassel**, the Queen consort of King Christian V of Denmark and mother of Frederick IV.\n\nNote: while the search confirmed Louise's own family background and her role as Danish Crown Princess, the retrieved chunks did not explicitly name her husband's mother, so the identification of Charlotte Amalie of Hesse-Kassel rests on the standard historical record of the Danish royal house rather than on a directly retrieved passage.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 61273.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:b126cad8f81aed3c5cc29c20c25b1adc7d1f33e1c4e264c3", "question": "Which film whose producer was born first, All-American Co-Ed or Lagu Kenangan?", "answers": ["All-American Co-Ed"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**All-American Co-Ed** is the film whose producer was born first.\n\n- **All-American Co-Ed** (1941) was produced by **Leroy Prinz**, who also directed it as a Hal Roach \"Streamliner\" for United Artists[1]. Prinz was born in 1895.\n- **Lagu Kenangan** (1953) was produced by **Djamaluddin Malik** for the Persari Film Corporation[7][8]. Malik was born in 1917.\n\nSince Leroy Prinz (1895) was born earlier than Djamaluddin Malik (1917), *All-American Co-Ed* is the answer.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 164388.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:2d1951b62f317038d28f6ac6a2b21e9d2e7f921ea528948b", "question": "Which country the performer of song I Believe In Your Sweet Love is from?", "answers": ["United Kingdom"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "\"I Believe in Your Sweet Love\" was performed by Bonnie Tyler, a Welsh singer[5]. Therefore, the performer is from the **United Kingdom** — she is Welsh (from Wales).", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 209632.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:314e76591d11d30d2bd59b2f12b671e873b786656f19956d", "question": "Where was the place of death of Agnes Of Hohenstaufen's husband?", "answers": ["Brunswick"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, Agnes of Hohenstaufen was married to **Henry V, Count Palatine of the Rhine**, the Welf count palatine [2].\n\nAs for his place of death: while the search results confirm the husband's identity as Henry V, they did not explicitly retrieve a document stating his place of death. According to standard historical records, Henry V, Count Palatine of the Rhine, died in **Braunschweig (Brunswick)**, the heartland of his family's Welf territories, in 1227.\n\nSo the answer is: **Braunschweig (Brunswick)**.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 93001.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:7140432f1c424674d04ea819fa63f85aa4f154d72ab66285", "question": "Who is Marcus Annius Libo's aunt?", "answers": ["Vibia Sabina"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, the answer concerns **Marcus Annius Libo (suffect consul in 161)**, whose aunt was the **Empress Faustina the Elder** (wife of Emperor Antoninus Pius).\n\nReasoning chain from the evidence:\n- The consul of 161 was the son of Marcus Annius Libo, consul in 128[3].\n- That father (the consul of 128) had an elder sister who was the Empress Faustina the Elder, mother of Faustina the Younger[4].\n- Therefore, Faustina the Elder was the paternal aunt of the younger Libo. This is corroborated by the fact that he was \"the nephew of emperor Antoninus Pius\"[2] — Antoninus Pius having married a sister from this family line[5].\n\nNote: If you meant the elder Marcus Annius Libo (consul in 128)[4], the retrieved documents do not explicitly name any aunt of his.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 85567.4, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:5421c1e591296d64636a7e99fbfe98dddfed0f83d2053380", "question": "Who is the mother of the director of film Dalida (2017 Film)?", "answers": ["Marie Laforêt"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The 2017 film *Dalida* was written, directed and co-produced by **Lisa Azuelos**[1]. Lisa Azuelos is the daughter of French singer and actress **Marie Laforêt** (and of Judas Azuelos)[6][7].\n\nSo, the mother of the film's director is **Marie Laforêt**.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 28056.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:188123e1b35a7de33fc44a40b55ab9ff0b59d29dc30f9148", "question": "What is the place of birth of the director of film A Chrysanthemum Bursts In Cincoesquinas?", "answers": ["Buenos Aires"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- The film *A Chrysanthemum Bursts in Cincoesquinas* (1998) was written and directed by **Daniel Burman**, in his feature film debut[1], and he is confirmed as the director[5].\n\nHowever, the knowledge base does not contain information about Daniel Burman's place of birth, so I cannot provide that detail from the available sources.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 214585.5, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:3292d2bcbbf8fc4816d168bcb7f81c13341198da1e88b903", "question": "Which film was released more recently, Bajo Otro Sol or Riding The California Trail?", "answers": ["Bajo Otro Sol"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Bajo Otro Sol** was released more recently.\n\n- *Bajo Otro Sol* is a 1988 Argentine film [1].\n- *Riding the California Trail* is a 1947 American Western film, released on January 11, 1947 by Monogram Pictures [6].\n\nSince 1988 comes after 1947, *Bajo Otro Sol* is the more recent film.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 103246.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:96500ef697df70106798988a9065594622cdeff67156cd20", "question": "When is Henrietta Maria Of Brandenburg-Schwedt's father's birthday?", "answers": ["May 19, 1669"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, Henrietta Maria of Brandenburg-Schwedt's father was **Philip William, Margrave of Brandenburg-Schwedt**, and he was born in **1669**[1]. \n\nNote: the knowledge base only records his birth year (1669) along with his death year (1711); it does not specify the exact day and month of his birth, so I cannot provide a more precise date from the available sources.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 29251.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:f67db35cb225c73bb753006bd14fab03942bbe0157a74979", "question": "Who is the spouse of the director of film Streets Of Blood?", "answers": ["Sandra Nelson"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n1. **Hop 1 — Director**: *Streets of Blood* is a 2009 direct-to-video action film directed by **Charles Winkler**, starring Val Kilmer, 50 Cent, Michael Biehn and Sharon Stone[2].\n\n2. **Hop 2 — Spouse**: Unfortunately, the knowledge base search did not return any evidence documenting Charles Winkler's spouse, so I cannot confirm who his spouse is from the available sources.\n\n**Answer**: The director of *Streets of Blood* is Charles Winkler[2], but his spouse's identity is not found in the retrieved knowledge base evidence, so I do not know that part of the answer.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 97435.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:5a867841d94c9f88f3bc0c333e93484486b09341db474bd6", "question": "Where was the place of death of Sancha Of Castile, Queen Of Navarre's mother?", "answers": ["Palencia"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on my searches, I was unable to retrieve sufficient evidence to answer this question. The knowledge base lookups confirmed documents about Sancha of Castile, Queen of Navarre exist (including references to her family tree and children), but the retrieved evidence did not identify who her mother was, nor did it provide any information about a place of death for her mother.\n\nSince the bridging evidence needed for this multi-hop question (the identity of Sancha's mother, followed by that person's place of death) could not be verified from the retrieved results, I cannot reliably answer where her mother died without inventing facts.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 102845.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:059802de84ebd63ee99284c9cb2b7db2d45ca66c55e68ee1", "question": "Which film was released more recently, Dance With A Stranger or Miley Naa Miley Hum?", "answers": ["Miley Naa Miley Hum"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Miley Naa Miley Hum** was released more recently.\n\n- **Miley Naa Miley Hum** is a 2011 Indian film directed by Tanveer Khan, released on **4 November 2011**[9].\n- **Dance with a Stranger** is the 1985 British film (its release year of 1985 predates 2011 by over two decades).\n\nSo Miley Naa Miley Hum (2011) came out much later than Dance with a Stranger (1985).", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 112248.2, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:5c3829f10f9daf565e9b5b52ca19f5c044550e916479da74", "question": "Which film has the director born later, Woman In The Moon or Changeland?", "answers": ["Changeland"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Changeland** has the director born later.\n\n- *Changeland* (2019) was written and directed by **Seth Green**, born in 1974[3].\n- *Woman in the Moon* is a much older silent-era film (1929), directed by **Fritz Lang**, who was born in 1890 — decades earlier than Seth Green.\n\nSo the director of *Changeland* (Seth Green) was born later than the director of *Woman in the Moon* (Fritz Lang).", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 99026.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:633204c891118a6f3d1ae62d7b444c2ee02ad0cbae4876cc", "question": "Which film has the director died later, Seven In The Sun or Daughter Of The Jungle?", "answers": ["Seven In The Sun"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Seven In The Sun** has the director who died later.\n\n- *Seven in the Sun* (1960 Italian adventure film) was written and directed by **Sergio Bergonzelli**, who died in 2002[10].\n- *Daughter of the Jungle* (1949 adventure film) was directed by **Jacques Tourneur**, who died in 1977[11][12].\n\nSince Bergonzelli (2002) died after Tourneur (1977), the film with the later-dying director is **Seven In The Sun**.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 226550.2, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:977f59ef09f7cc4ad6c71fc18d8b60e818e07a43cd7bee92", "question": "Which film was released first, Vacations In Majorca or Dr. Socrates?", "answers": ["Dr. Socrates"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Dr. Socrates** was released first. It came out in **1935**[6], while *Vacations in Majorca* was released in **1959**[1] — a difference of 24 years.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 239714.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:85d2e8c38cc3b6f464eae6d84ef2df5f41807c9f8bf3aac8", "question": "Who is the spouse of the performer of song This Time (Waylon Jennings Song)?", "answers": ["Jessi Colter"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- The song **\"This Time\"** was written and recorded by American country music artist **Waylon Jennings**, released in April 1974 as the title track of the album *This Time* and reaching No. 1 on the Billboard Hot Country Singles chart[1].\n\n- As for his spouse(s): according to the knowledge base, Jennings **was married four times**[4]. The named spouses are:\n  - **Maxine Caroll Lawrence** (married in 1956, mother of four of his children)[4]\n  - **Lynne Jones** (married December 10, 1962; divorced in 1967)[4]\n  - **Barbara Elizabeth Rood** (married in 1967, the same year as his divorce from Lynne Jones)[4]\n\nNotably, Jennings composed \"This Time\" about the trials and tribulations of his marriages and divorces[4]. The name of his fourth wife is not mentioned in the retrieved documents, so I cannot confirm it from the available evidence.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 156171.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:c94e0220a7c5dadee3094df576df766b6d1a15b6c6e21011", "question": "Which film has the director who died earlier, Melody Of The World or Ladies Love Danger?", "answers": ["Melody Of The World"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Melody of the World** is directed by Walter Ruttmann[1][3], while **Ladies Love Danger** was directed by H. Bruce Humberstone[7].\n\nWalter Ruttmann died in 1941, whereas H. Bruce Humberstone lived until 1984 — so the film whose director died earlier is **Melody of the World**.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 235444.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:cab5465c3f7663e5d72c15a32bc04c8a917dac3c03828814", "question": "Where was the place of death of the composer of film Miracle Of Marcelino?", "answers": ["Madrid"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- The film **Miracle of Marcelino** (1955 Spanish film) had its musical score and theme song composed by **Pablo Sorozábal**[1].\n\nAs for Sorozábal's place of death, the retrieved evidence does not explicitly state it. Based on general knowledge, Pablo Sorozábal died in **Madrid, Spain** (in 1988), but this detail could not be verified against the available retrieved documents before the search limit was reached.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 217072.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:a88430cef36a0222c3c30780328ff266b16325a7ec723a97", "question": "Where was the place of death of Shahnawaz Bhutto's mother?", "answers": ["Dubai"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Shahnawaz Bhutto's mother was **Nusrat Bhutto** (Begum Nusrat Bhutto), wife of Zulfiqar Ali Bhutto[3]. She died at the **Iranian Hospital in Dubai** (United Arab Emirates) on 23 October 2011, at the age of 82[6].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 110901.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:0c43156b7d6bc17425a89dc6c6d48fc8c2c72ac9eba55a87", "question": "Are Gut (Crișul Alb) and Gepiș both located in the same country?", "answers": ["yes"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Yes. Both are located in the same country — Romania:\n\n- The **Gut** (also known as Condratău) is a left tributary of the river Crișul Alb in **Romania**, discharging into the Crișul Alb near Șicula.[1]\n- The **Gepiș** is a right tributary of the river Crișul Repede in **Romania**, discharging into the Crișul Repede in Groși.[4]", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 82917.6, "error": ""}
