{"qid": "2wikimqa:9ef1c9e836fb3844fe16369a346088af89b8da29e24aab1f", "question": "Who is Sir William Gore, 3Rd Baronet's paternal grandfather?", "answers": ["Sir Paul Gore, 1st Baronet"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on my searches, I was unable to retrieve sufficient verified evidence to answer this question definitively.\n\nWhat I found:\n- The knowledge base does contain material on **Sir William Gore, 3rd Baronet** as part of a collection on British aristocratic families [wiki topic: British Historical Figures], including a noted relationship question connecting him to **William Ormsby-Gore**.\n- However, the retrieved evidence snippets did not include the specific biographical/genealogical details naming Sir William Gore's father or paternal grandfather, so I cannot confirm the identity of his paternal grandfather from the retrieved sources.\n\nI therefore cannot reliably state who Sir William Gore, 3rd Baronet's paternal grandfather was based on the evidence currently retrieved, and I'd rather not speculate without supporting documentation.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 183816.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:9c5350cca5afdd1a7254dbc26b3642401551473f4b071ce6", "question": "Which film came out earlier, The Drover'S Sweetheart or Pigsty (Film)?", "answers": ["The Drover'S Sweetheart"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**The Drover's Sweetheart** came out earlier.\n\n- *The Drover's Sweetheart* is a **1911** film made by Agnes and John Gavin (though it's considered lost and it's uncertain if it was ever even released commercially)[1].\n- *Pigsty* (Italian: *Porcile*) is a **1969** Italian film written and directed by Pier Paolo Pasolini[9].\n\nSo The Drover's Sweetheart predates Pigsty by nearly six decades.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 175863.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:62453a76a4867b6d09ac435581e1a327ec5b55cf231c79f9", "question": "Which film has the director who died earlier, Il Gaucho or Bomgay?", "answers": ["Bomgay"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Bomgay** is the film whose director died earlier.\n\n- **Il Gaucho** was directed by **Dino Risi**[2], who died on 7 June 2018.\n- **Bomgay** was directed by **Riyad Vinci Wadia and Jangu Sethna**[8]; Riyad Vinci Wadia died in December 2003, at age 35.\n\nSince Riyad Vinci Wadia's death (2003) predates Dino Risi's (2018), **Bomgay** has the director who died earlier.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 50618.2, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:884614fa7d0fe723587d2f2677d3f2143cd13ab74391bea6", "question": "Where was the wife of Lou Breslow born?", "answers": ["Dayton, Ohio"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, Lou Breslow's wife was **Marion Byron**, a film actress and comedian whom he married in 1932 and remained married to until her death in 1985[2]. \n\nHowever, the retrieved evidence does not include information about where Marion Byron was born, so I cannot confirm her birthplace from the knowledge base.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 481696.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:c1b46a5458b15fdbfcd264b7e26e42d2cbaafb0e6dc5f48d", "question": "Are both directors of films La Morte Vivante and Stranger On Horseback from the same country?", "answers": ["yes"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "No. Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- **La Morte Vivante** is described as a 1982 **French** horror-drama film directed by **Jean Rollin**[4].\n- **Stranger on Horseback** is described as a 1955 **American** Western film directed by **Jacques Tourneur**[6].\n\nSo the two directors are associated with films from different countries — one French and one American — meaning they are not from the same country.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 60478.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:98ead8987446388d37301c03d7d9f24e2f511a9e0c10bcdf", "question": "What is the cause of death of Constantia Eriksdotter's father?", "answers": ["poisoning"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Constantia Eriksdotter's father was **Eric XIV of Sweden** — she was his illegitimate daughter with Agda Persdotter [1].\n\nRegarding his death: Eric XIV (13 December 1533 – 26 February 1577) reigned as King of Sweden from 1560 until he was captured in a rebellion led by his brother John in 1568 and formally deposed on 26 January 1569 [5]. He then died on 26 February 1577 [5].\n\nHowever, the knowledge base does not explicitly state the precise cause of his death (i.e., the specific manner in which he died), so I cannot confirm that detail beyond noting that he died about eight years after being deposed and imprisoned following his brother's rebellion.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 128264.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:c9e8d02824dfbdf95fe9f90c45dc13bc12f45b6969b1467b", "question": "Which film came out earlier, X-Paroni or Mi Novia Está De Madre?", "answers": ["X-Paroni"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**X-Paroni** came out earlier.\n\n- X-Paroni is a 1964 Finnish comedy film, notable as Spede Pasanen's debut in a leading role and as co-writer/director of a full-length film[1].\n- Mi novia está de madre is a Dominican comedy released in the summer of 2007, starring Roberto Salcedo, Patricia Manterola, and Eddy Herrera[6].\n\nThat makes X-Paroni (1964) about 43 years older than Mi Novia Está De Madre (2007).", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 55400.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:eb1478ef3d4926564e153e99fd139c87e59cfaee49caac88", "question": "Who is the father-in-law of Hong Ra-Hee?", "answers": ["Lee Byung-chul"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Hong Ra-hee's father-in-law was Lee Byung-chul**, the founder of the Samsung Group.\n\nReasoning chain from the knowledge base:\n- Hong Ra-hee was married to Lee Kun-hee (she is described as his widow) [3][8].\n- Lee Kun-hee \"was the third son of Lee Byung-chul, the founder of the Samsung group\" [6][7].\n\nSo her father-in-law — the father of her husband Lee Kun-hee — is Samsung founder **Lee Byung-chul**.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 119406.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:259e029da053a54f862f2455f3b92fb5f1b810647f1c1825", "question": "Who is Isabella Of Bourbon's paternal grandfather?", "answers": ["John I, Duke of Bourbon"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- Isabella of Bourbon (c. 1434 – 25 September 1465), Countess of Charolais, was the second wife of Charles the Bold, and she was **a daughter of Charles I, Duke of Bourbon and Agnes of Burgundy**[5]. Another excerpt confirms she was the daughter of the reigning Duke of Bourbon and his Burgundian wife Agnes, daughter of John the Fearless[3].\n\nSo her father (through whom the paternal line runs) was **Charles I, Duke of Bourbon**. However, the retrieved documents do not explicitly name the father of Charles I, Duke of Bourbon, so the knowledge base does not allow me to confirm who Isabella of Bourbon's paternal grandfather was. Based on what I could verify, I can only identify her father, not her paternal grandfather.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 310435.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:8af3f07b73fabc0cc4ef4e6928818d1ff08ead9f41a5085a", "question": "Are Ding Yaping and Johann Christian Gustav Lucae of the same nationality?", "answers": ["yes"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Yes — they share the German nationality. Johann Christian Gustav Lucae (1814–1885) was a German anatomist from Frankfurt am Main[6]. Ding Yaping (born 1967) is a former international table tennis player who is described as both Chinese and German — she won women's doubles bronze medals at the 1989 and 1991 World Table Tennis Championships for China before later representing Germany[1]. So while Ding Yaping has dual Chinese–German nationality, both she and Lucae hold German nationality in common.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 107018.4, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:3816f7d8e90a5497a1c0e415bf25218037c690e8e4d0d016", "question": "Which country Dorothea Of Denmark, Duchess Of Mecklenburg's father is from?", "answers": ["Norway"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Dorothea of Denmark, Duchess of Mecklenburg's father was **King Frederick I of Denmark**[2], so her father was from **Denmark**.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 90417.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:b8ffb375e75ee2976b8825d05d48c34638c7ffeb6d67baff", "question": "Who is the paternal grandfather of Diego Fernández De Oviedo?", "answers": ["Flaín Muñoz"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, Diego Fernández de Oviedo was the son of **Fernando Flaínez** (and Elvira Peláez)[1]. However, the knowledge base documents do not explicitly name his paternal grandfather by full identity.\n\nWhat can be noted:\n- His father was Fernando Flaínez[1].\n- Following medieval Iberian patronymic naming custom, the surname \"Flaínez\" means \"son of Flaín,\" which indicates Diego's paternal grandfather bore the name **Flaín** — but the retrieved documents do not provide further details about him.\n- The only other ancestor named in the evidence is Count **Fernando Bermúdez de Cea**, described as Diego's great-grandfather (shared with King Ferdinand I), though the lineage path is not specified in the source[1].\n\nSo, per the available records, the paternal grandfather can only be identified as \"Flaín\" by naming convention; no additional verified details about him appear in the knowledge base.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 435897.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:0cf27c68148c99571860af561ce5f64c4524fde278defc63", "question": "Who died first, Frederick Cleveland Morgan or Nathaniel Mclenaghan?", "answers": ["Nathaniel Mclenaghan"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Nathaniel McLenaghan died first.**\n\n- Nathaniel McLenaghan died at Perth in **1912** [2]\n- Frederick Cleveland Morgan died in Senneville on **October 3, 1962** [1]", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 19864.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:025911ff0afd34976b0a800c198c4117f95edfcd7b64bb24", "question": "What is the cause of death of Heonjong Of Goryeo's father?", "answers": ["illness"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- Heonjong of Goryeo (r. 1094–1095) was the eldest son of **King Seonjong**, the 13th king of Goryeo[1][7].\n- However, the knowledge base does not document a specific cause of death for Seonjong — his cause of death is listed as **unknown**[10].\n\nSo, the cause of death of Heonjong's father, King Seonjong, is not recorded in the available sources.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 431930.0, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:550f734c7ef908fcfe6b1b7e761826340f00abaa5eb305a0", "question": "Which film whose director is younger, Cuchillos De Fuego or A Woman Has Killed?", "answers": ["Cuchillos De Fuego"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Cuchillos de Fuego** is the film whose director is younger.\n\nBased on the retrieved evidence:\n- *Cuchillos de fuego* (1990 Venezuelan film) was directed by **Román Chalbaud**[1]\n- *A Woman Has Killed* (1952 Italian film) was directed by **Vittorio Cottafavi**[7]\n\nComparing their birth dates: Román Chalbaud was born in 1931, while Vittorio Cottafavi was born in 1914, making Chalbaud — the director of *Cuchillos de Fuego* — the younger of the two.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 479961.5, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:3ee59c959e64a29c8a30263816ad47b76ffab36e5b8859ee", "question": "What is the place of birth of the director of film Ninamaninja Kalpadukal?", "answers": ["Methala"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The director of *Ninamaninja Kalpadukal* (1963 Malayalam film) is **N. N. Pisharody**[1][3]. He was born into a feudal family known as \"Kallil\" in **Methala, near Perumbavoor, Kerala**[4].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 108142.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:43cf26663f3b4cec7a8ea68d56909201a2d1b1ad82512190", "question": "Which film came out earlier, Alkohol or Night Of Dark Shadows?", "answers": ["Alkohol"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Alkohol** came out earlier. It is a 1919 German silent drama film directed by Ewald André Dupont and Alfred Lind, which premiered at the Marmorhaus in Berlin [2]. *Night of Dark Shadows* was released much later — filming began on March 29, 1971 under the title *Curse of Dark Shadows* before being retitled for its 1971 release [7].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 106704.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:f0523a41000b43996413780968b611c3f4d28b87f4acc859", "question": "Are Revolt In The Big House and The Fugitive (1914 Film) from the same country?", "answers": ["no"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "No, they are not from the same country.\n\n- **Revolt in the Big House** is a 1958 **American** film noir directed by R. G. Springsteen, starring Gene Evans, Robert Blake and Timothy Carey, with portions shot at Folsom State Prison in California[3].\n- **The Fugitive** (Russian: Беглец) is a 1914 **Russian-French** short film directed by Alexandre Volkoff[10].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 109604.2, "error": ""}
