{"qid": "2wikimqa:efea9c05de081efb7ef76741d3f24da2e993d54d99677b72", "question": "When was Antoine Philippe, Duke Of Montpensier's mother born?", "answers": ["13 March 1753"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Antoine Philippe, Duke of Montpensier's mother was **Louise Marie Adélaïde de Bourbon, Duchess of Orléans** — she was the wife of Louis Philippe, Duke of Orléans (\"Philippe Égalité\") and mother of Antoine Philippe as well as of Louis Philippe, later King of the French[2].\n\nRegarding her exact birth date: the retrieved knowledge base documents confirm her identity as his mother[2], but do not contain her date of birth. According to standard historical records, Louise Marie Adélaïde de Bourbon was born on **13 March 1753**, though I could not verify this specific date within the available knowledge base sources.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "entity_relation_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 410954.2, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:6a60fa19187345478a447b63d8f52a1cb5341e964cda29db", "question": "Where was the composer of film Consenting Adults (1992 Film) born?", "answers": ["New York"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The composer of the 1992 film *Consenting Adults* was **Michael Small**, who composed the film's original music score[2]. He was born in **New York City** (though he grew up in Maplewood, New Jersey)[7].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 43898.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:24a43c1b071d8bb99f51fec368dbc438cf7aea1f549ea195", "question": "Which film came out first, F The Prom or The Comedians Of Comedy?", "answers": ["The Comedians Of Comedy"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**The Comedians of Comedy** came out first.\n\n- *The Comedians of Comedy* was shot in the fall of 2004 and had its world premiere at the South by Southwest film festival in March 2005[8].\n- *F the Prom* is a 2017 film, released online and on-demand on December 5, 2017[1].\n\nSo The Comedians of Comedy preceded F the Prom by about 12 years.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 50993.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:435fae9b23d8b22e85a57cfd8ceb8541dea5b0c551acc3a9", "question": "Which film has the director who died later, True To The Navy or No Trees In The Street?", "answers": ["No Trees In The Street"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**No Trees In The Street** is the film whose director died later.\n\n- *True to the Navy* (1930) was directed by **Frank Tuttle**[5], who died in 1973.\n- *No Trees in the Street* (1959) was directed by **J. Lee Thompson**[7][8], who died in 2002.\n\nSince J. Lee Thompson (d. 2002) outlived Frank Tuttle (d. 1973), *No Trees In The Street* has the director who died later.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 472507.8, "error": ""}
