{"qid": "2wikimqa:300ccba91f776e583d418d6d9ecc5e1bdca7bd80580cd36e", "question": "Was Dudley Russell or Juan René Serrano born first?", "answers": ["Dudley Russell"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Dudley Russell was born first.**\n\n- **Juan René Serrano** was born on **23 February 1984** in Guadalajara, Jalisco, Mexico; he is a Mexican archer[6].\n- **Dudley Russell**'s biographical entry covers an early career, service in **World War II**, post-war activities, and honours/decorations[2][3][4][5]. Someone whose documented career centers on World War II necessarily lived as an adult during the 1930s–1940s, meaning he was born many decades before 1984.\n\nSo even though the exact birth date for Dudley Russell wasn't fully captured in the retrieved snippets, it is clear from his World War II-era biography that he was born long before Juan René Serrano (born 1984).", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 177711.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:f5cf6d94b9e4e7adfc30d262396bc29e201d9e07ead1d088", "question": "Which magazine was established first, Women'S Suffrage Journal or Mostar (Magazine)?", "answers": ["Women'S Suffrage Journal"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Women's Suffrage Journal** was established first.\n\n- The **Women's Suffrage Journal** was founded by Lydia Becker and Jessie Boucherett in **1870**, ceasing publication in 1890 after Becker's death [1].\n- The magazine **Mostar** began publishing in **March 2005** [6].\n\nSo the Women's Suffrage Journal predates Mostar by about 135 years.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 41957.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:544828db02efd1313bfc0a1bdeb8c3df5985c299254b0222", "question": "Where was the director of film The Dinner (2013 Film) born?", "answers": ["Eindhoven"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, **The Dinner (2013)** (Dutch: *Het Diner*) was written and directed by **Menno Meyjes**[5].\n\nHowever, the retrieved search results only confirm the director's identity — they do not include any information about Menno Meyjes' birthplace, so I cannot verify where he was born from the knowledge base evidence available here. (For reference, public biographical sources generally list him as born in Bloemendaal, Netherlands, but this specific detail was not confirmed in the retrieved documents.)", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 114470.2, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:bf2899717e8d7d3d83d865ca5ff59e26d7f647e6025e2d52", "question": "Where was the father of Muhammad Al-Nasir born?", "answers": ["Morocco"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, Muhammad al-Nasir (the fourth Almohad Caliph, r. 1199–1213) was the son of Abu Yusuf Yaqub al-Mansur, who died on 25 January 1199[3][5]. However, the retrieved documents do not contain any information about where Abu Yusuf Yaqub al-Mansur was born, so I cannot confirm his birthplace from the available evidence.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 152072.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:e15605da0c5b6f02c85aff9f1f683d3f85d211c083792ecb", "question": "Do both films, The Glass Castle (1950 Film) and The Ferret (Film), have the directors who are from the same country?", "answers": ["yes"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "**Yes** — both films were directed by French directors.\n\n- **The Glass Castle (1950)** — *Le Château de verre* — was directed by **René Clément**, as listed in his filmography[2].\n- **The Ferret** (*Le furet*) is described as \"a 1950 French crime film directed by **Raymond Leboursier**\"[9].\n\nBoth are 1950 French-language films (*Le Château de verre*, *Le furet*) helmed by French directors, so their directors come from the same country: France.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 211424.6, "error": ""}
