{"qid": "2wikimqa:7a35ba110f4c26f7eb9d4dcc2e8c1baac383c777f0904976", "question": "Which film has the director who was born earlier, Khud-Daar or Murderer In The Fog?", "answers": ["Murderer In The Fog"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- **Khud-Daar** (1982 Indian Hindi action film) was directed by **Ravi Tandon**[1]. He died on 11 February 2022 at age 86, just six days before his 87th birthday, which places his birth around **February 1935**[2].\n- **Murderer in the Fog** (1964 West German crime film) was directed by **Eugen York**[6]. However, the retrieved evidence does not include Eugen York's date of birth, so I cannot verify his birth year from the knowledge base.\n\n**Conclusion:** From the verified evidence alone, only Ravi Tandon's approximate birth year (1935) is confirmed; Eugen York's birth date was not found in the retrieved documents. For reference, Eugen York is generally known to have been born in 1912, which would make **Murderer in the Fog** the film with the earlier-born director — but this relies on outside knowledge rather than retrieved evidence.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 55772.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:a7d0cfa55dce1e96490d1e6c0188398864724e96a44e4b79", "question": "Who is the paternal grandfather of Sir John Hamilton-Dalrymple, 5Th Baronet?", "answers": ["Sir Hew Dalrymple, 2nd Baronet"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, I can establish part of this chain, but not the final step:\n\n- Sir John Hamilton-Dalrymple, 5th Baronet succeeded **his brother**, Sir Hew Dalrymple-Hamilton, 4th Baronet, in the baronetcy[1].\n- The 4th Baronet was the eldest son of **Sir Hew Dalrymple, 3rd Baronet**[2], which means the 5th Baronet's father was therefore Sir Hew Dalrymple, 3rd Baronet.\n\nHowever, the retrieved evidence does not identify who Sir Hew Dalrymple, 3rd Baronet's own father was — which would be the paternal grandfather of the 5th Baronet. So I cannot give a definitive name for the paternal grandfather from the knowledge base; I can only confirm that the 5th Baronet's father was Sir Hew Dalrymple, 3rd Baronet.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 135887.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:b9a9b860c0f0430853d1db2756095da274d522beed2acbeb", "question": "Who is the spouse of the director of film Soldier (1998 American Film)?", "answers": ["Milla"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n1. **Director of Soldier**: The 1998 American science fiction action film *Soldier* was directed by **Paul W. S. Anderson**[6].\n\n2. **Spouse**: The knowledge base results did not include a document explicitly confirming his spouse's identity, so I cannot verify this from the retrieved evidence alone. However, based on general knowledge, Paul W. S. Anderson's spouse is **Milla Jovovich** (the actress and model), whom he married in 2009.\n\nSo the answer is **Milla Jovovich** — though please note this second hop could not be confirmed within this knowledge base's retrieved documents.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 135677.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:49035ecce6e78a355307dd6a1ddb11a87cab76090d655d2f", "question": "Which film has the director who was born first, The Longshots or Station For Two?", "answers": ["Station For Two"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Station For Two** has the director who was born first.\n\n- *Station for Two* (1983) was directed by **Eldar Ryazanov**[9][7], who was born on November 18, 1927.\n- *The Longshots* (2008) was directed by **Fred Durst**[1], who was born on August 20, 1970.\n\nSince Ryazanov (1927) predates Durst (1970), Station For Two is the film whose director was born first.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 180030.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:8848d4bd1425f8bef31b6c279ec378bcbca14f10b702c4ea", "question": "When did Thomas Of Galloway (Bastard)'s father die?", "answers": ["1234"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, Thomas of Galloway (bastard) was an illegitimate son of **Alan of Galloway**, Constable of Scotland and the last Mac Fearghusa Lord of Galloway[1]. After Alan's death—having left no legitimate sons—King Alexander II of Scotland planned to divide the lordship among the husbands of Alan's three daughters[1].\n\nHowever, the retrieved documents do not specify the exact year of Alan of Galloway's death, so I cannot confirm the precise date from the available evidence.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 152584.0, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:72132e87102859b583fb69a8a2a6a8b026be4fec5a1437e0", "question": "When did Robert Bertie, 3Rd Earl Of Lindsey's father die?", "answers": ["25 July 1666"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Robert Bertie, 3rd Earl of Lindsey's father was **Montagu Bertie, 2nd Earl of Lindsey**, who died in **1666**.\n\nThis can be inferred from the retrieved evidence: Robert Bertie was styled \"Lord Willoughby de Eresby\" (the heir-apparent title) only *from 1642 to 1666*, after which he succeeded as the 3rd Earl of Lindsey [1] — indicating his father, the 2nd Earl, died in 1666 and he inherited the earldom then.\n\nFor additional context, his grandfather, Robert Bertie, 1st Earl of Lindsey, died earlier, on 24 October 1642 [2], which is when the 2nd Earl (Robert's father) succeeded to the title.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 128827.5, "error": ""}
