{"qid": "hotpotqa:220230ff5154e6f0ccad63965d06ce69a9226bd72cc32fa4", "question": "McLaren MP4/11 was driven by what Finnish former professional racing driver", "answers": ["Mika Häkkinen"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Mika Häkkinen** was the Finnish former professional racing driver who drove the McLaren MP4/11.\n\nEvidence from the knowledge base confirms this: Mika Pauli Häkkinen, nicknamed \"The Flying Finn,\" is a Finnish former racing driver[1] who joined McLaren in 1993 as a test driver before being promoted to the race team[2], and remained with McLaren through the mid-1990s — the period of the MP4/11 (1996 season) — going on to win back-to-back World Drivers' Championships with McLaren in 1998 and 1999[1].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 68698.0, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:01aff89f9ce55470c12450b595c268a225a638582dac204f", "question": "Which of the movie which has Rich Lee 3-D previsualizations was directed by Francis Lawrence?", "answers": ["Constantine"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Constantine** (2005).\n\nAccording to the retrieved evidence, Rich Lee created 3‑D previsualizations for big-budget Hollywood films including the first three *Pirates of the Caribbean* films, *I Am Legend*, *Minority Report*, and *Constantine*[1]. Of these, the one directed by Francis Lawrence is *Constantine* — the other listed films were helmed by different directors (*Pirates of the Caribbean* by Gore Verbinski, *Minority Report* by Steven Spielberg).", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 111514.4, "error": ""}
