{"qid": "hotpotqa:4b753aee2d76b79f12f1b8708dd61bde51405af6fe602520", "question": "H-63 is a highway that runs near the county seat of what Michigan county?", "answers": ["Chippewa County"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "H-63 (Mackinac Trail) is a county-designated highway in Michigan's Upper Peninsula that runs from north of St. Ignace in Mackinac County up into Chippewa County, ending on the south side of Sault Ste. Marie[3][4]. The county it runs near the county seat of is **Chippewa County** — Sault Ste. Marie, where H-63 terminates, is the county seat of Chippewa County, Michigan[1][3].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "entity_relation_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 42903.4, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:019dbd177ddcff6752aaabc8c0e459f3ae4003f718bd672b", "question": "Kevin Yorn an American entertainment attorney who represents an Australian actor who  played the role of Josh Taylor in what soap opera?", "answers": ["Neighbours"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Neighbours.**\n\nThe reasoning chain:\n1. Kevin Yorn is an American entertainment attorney and co-founder/managing partner of the Yorn Barnes Levine Entertainment Law Firm [6].\n2. The Australian actor he represents is Liam Hemsworth, who \"played the roles of Josh Taylor in the soap opera **Neighbours**\" (as well as Marcus in *The Elephant Princess*) [1].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 114652.4, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:07f505d321fd7a7c04e158059cb69ac3ac7ecdebfb03037d", "question": "What is the day of the horse race of which ESPN covers both the post position draw and the undercard races?", "answers": ["Saturday"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, ESPN/ESPN2's thoroughbred racing coverage included \"the post position draw for the Kentucky Derby and Preakness Stakes\" as well as \"the Kentucky Derby and Belmont Stakes undercard races\" and \"the Preakness undercard races\"[2].\n\nSo the races for which ESPN covers **both** the post position draw and the undercard races are the **Kentucky Derby** and the **Preakness Stakes** (the Belmont Stakes only gets undercard coverage). Both of these races are run on a **Saturday** — the Kentucky Derby on the first Saturday in May and the Preakness Stakes on the third Saturday in May.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 160861.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:c9f8b2166f7c44bf2e0843b2c77fb9fa5738af275555ca73", "question": "Which ocean would the ingredients likely come from for the She-crab soup?", "answers": ["Atlantic Ocean"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The ingredients would likely come from the **Atlantic Ocean**. She-crab soup is made with Atlantic blue crab meat, along with milk or heavy cream, crab or fish stock, and traditionally crab roe [1]. It's a regional specialty of the South Carolina Lowcountry, commonly featured in Charleston, South Carolina and Savannah, Georgia restaurants — coastal areas on the Atlantic seaboard where the blue crabs are harvested [1].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 85739.2, "error": ""}
