{"qid": "hotpotqa:4567b6935bf5c64a1974b1089d67d176d9acac6b29836cb7", "question": "The 2011 La Manga Cup was won by Viking, who beat which Norwegian football club from the town of Kristiansand, currently playing in Tippeligaen having been promoted from Adeccoligaen in 2012?", "answers": ["IK Start"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**IK Start** — the Norwegian club from Kristiansand.\n\nReasoning from the retrieved evidence: the 2011 La Manga Cup featured Viking and Strømsgodset among its participating Tippeligaen sides, and Viking went on to win the tournament by beating IK Start in the final. Start matches the description in the question exactly: it is the football club from the town of Kristiansand, and it returned to the top flight by winning promotion from the Adeccoligaen (in 2012), putting it back in the Tippeligaen.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 143092.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:7d3bc2e36b406094cb586b4eeb07f13a7f1ac9dfbdce7d1f", "question": "Which composer was wrote his music most recently, Michael Tippett or Luigi Cherubini?", "answers": ["Michael Kemp Tippett"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Michael Tippett** wrote his music most recently.\n\n- Michael Tippett (1905–1998) was an English composer who lived and composed well into the 20th century, dying on 8 January 1998.[2][4]\n- Luigi Cherubini (1760–1842) was an Italian Classical/Romantic composer who died in Paris in 1842 at age 81.[6][7]\n\nSince Tippett's active period extended over 150 years beyond Cherubini's death, Tippett wrote his music far more recently.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 40507.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:d3249d0550c7105bdd4ed60c9ca9d955db08d362574c2086", "question": "Leonard Logsdail had a cameo role in the biographical film directed by whom?", "answers": ["Martin Scorsese"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Leonard Logsdail — the Manhattan-based bespoke tailor — has had cameo acting roles as a tailor in several films, including *The Wolf of Wall Street*, *Wall Street 2: Money Never Sleeps*, and *The Good Shepherd*[3]. Among these, the biographical film is *The Wolf of Wall Street*, which was directed by **Martin Scorsese** — one of the directors with whom Logsdail has collaborated[3].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 103911.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:c274ce731f680eb107c70386e2e341615378165ecc22799e", "question": "What Lithuanian producer is best known for a song that was one of the most popular songs in Ibiza in 2014?", "answers": ["Ten Walls"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Ten Walls** — the stage name of Lithuanian producer Marijus Adomaitis. His song \"Walking with Elephants,\" released in April 2014 by the German label BOSO, peaked at number 6 on the UK Singles Chart and was one of the most popular songs in Ibiza in 2014[2].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 130514.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "hotpotqa:6c64a81fa526cb96d0a191d9cbd85a7e917b5d4f03b316d7", "question": "The player who laid motionless for ten minutes in the Todd Bertuzzi–Steve Moore incident was born in which year ?", "answers": ["1978"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The player who lay motionless on the ice for ten minutes after being attacked by Todd Bertuzzi was **Steve Moore** — he was knocked unconscious during the March 8, 2004 game and carried off on a stretcher after roughly ten minutes[1][4].\n\nSteve Moore was born in **1978**.\n\n(Note: the retrieved evidence confirms Moore was the player left motionless for ten minutes[1][4]; his 1978 birth year is from general biographical knowledge, as the retrieved passages did not explicitly include his date of birth.)", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 163466.6, "error": ""}
