{"qid": "musique:685f8561239902c340fcf6b70d5ddc919b62aaf2b543ae3f", "question": "When was the last time Peter Till's sports team beat the winner of the 1894-95 FA Cup?", "answers": ["1 December 2010"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the evidence I was able to retrieve, here is what the knowledge base establishes:\n\n**Step 1 – Peter Till's sports team:** Peter Till (born 7 September 1985) is an English former professional footballer who played as a winger [2][3]; his clubs included **Birmingham City** [4][5] (and later Fleetwood Town [1]).\n\n**Step 2 – Winner of the 1894–95 FA Cup:** The cup was won by **Aston Villa**, who defeated West Bromwich Albion 1–0 in the final at Crystal Palace in London — Villa's second FA Cup victory [10].\n\n**Step 3 – When Birmingham City last beat Aston Villa:** Unfortunately, my retrieval allowance was exhausted before I could pull evidence of the Birmingham City vs. Aston Villa head-to-head results (the \"Second City derby\") from the knowledge base, so I cannot confirm the exact date of their last meeting won by Birmingham City using only retrieved sources.\n\nFrom general football knowledge (not verifiable against this knowledge base), Birmingham City's most recent competitive win over Aston Villa is commonly cited as **10 March 2019**, a 1–0 home victory in the EFL Championship — but please treat that date as unverified here, since no retrieved document confirms it.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 132205.1, "error": ""}
