{"qid": "musique:8267f95a2928cb63203d20da0079d98138d4f58281fc4e9e", "question": "When did the party who gained control of congress in the midterm elections in 1946 take control of the determiner of rules of the US House and US Senate?", "answers": ["January 2015"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Answer:** The party was the **Republican Party**, which gained control of both chambers of Congress in the November 1946 midterm elections during President Truman's first term[1]. It formally took over as the rule‑setting majority in each chamber when the **80th United States Congress convened on January 3, 1947** — from that point the GOP controlled the House and Senate, including the majority power to determine each chamber's rules, and (per related records) later held unified control of both Congress and the presidency[1][2].\n\n- [1] 1946 U.S. House elections topic map: Republican Party gained control of both chambers; key entities include the 80th United States Congress.\n- [2] Entity relations for the Republican Party: records of its taking control of the Senate and of unified Republican control of Congress.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 316634.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:fe052f64d5c1f66bd84e1f2dc6df342b1ea10d2763c22a90", "question": "What pantheon is the God of the underworld in ancient Egypt a part of?", "answers": ["ancient Egyptian religion"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The God of the underworld in ancient Egypt is **Osiris** — he was the judge and lord of the dead and the underworld, as well as a god of fertility, agriculture, the afterlife, resurrection, life, and vegetation[1].\n\nHe is part of the **ancient Egyptian pantheon** (the deities of ancient Egyptian religion)[1]. Within that pantheon, he was considered at times the eldest son of the earth god Geb and the sky goddess Nut, brother and husband of Isis, and brother of Set and Nephthys[1].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 48256.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:05f1867336770bf201cf9a88de60e2b9bdd893efe98d9593", "question": "What is the record label for the band which performed Pythons?", "answers": ["Kanine Records"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Sire Records.**\n\n\"Pythons\" is the second studio album by the indie rock band Surfer Blood, and it was released in June 2013 under Sire Records (produced by Gil Norton)[5].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 64311.3, "error": ""}
