{"qid": "musique:e5d8a267444a8532a875af8cfb8b07e6f6d02d6e85148540", "question": "What is the life expectancy of the type of retriever named after the body of water the Patuxent River turns into?", "answers": ["average lifespan at 9.4 years"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The retriever in question is the **Chesapeake Bay Retriever** — the Patuxent River is a tributary that empties into the Chesapeake Bay[1][5].\n\nRegarding its life expectancy:\n- A UK Kennel Club survey puts the median lifespan at **10.75 years** (average 9.85 years)[6]\n- A US breed club survey puts the average lifespan at **9.4 years**, with 1 in 4 dogs living to 13 years or more, while about 1 in 5 don't live past 5 years[6]", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 115518.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:648de9dea3ad81e8ac733acd312913385129ab16dd091834", "question": "Who is the president of the newly declared independent country that is part of the Commission of Truth and Friendship with the country where Sambas is located?", "answers": ["Francisco Guterres"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, the reasoning chain is:\n\n1. **Sambas** is located in **Indonesia** (Sambas Regency, West Kalimantan).\n2. Indonesia is one party to the **Indonesia–Timor Leste Commission of Truth and Friendship**, whose counterpart is **East Timor (Timor-Leste)** — the country that newly declared independence from Indonesia in 2002[1][3].\n3. Upon its independence, the president of East Timor was **Xanana Gusmão**, who served as the newly independent nation's first president.\n\nSo, the answer is **Xanana Gusmão**, president of newly independent East Timor (Timor-Leste), which formed the Commission of Truth and Friendship with Indonesia (where Sambas is located).", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 130975.4, "error": ""}
