{"qid": "musique:f6564f948dc28ef7be445d610eb42c1a6a6042d47e62e7a6", "question": "A participant of the Battle of Brechin is an instance of?", "answers": ["Scottish clan"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n**Participants** of the Battle of Brechin (fought 18 May 1452 during the reign of James II of Scotland) included **Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly**, who led the royalist forces of Clan Gordon and Clan Ogilvy to victory, and his defeated opponent **Alexander Lindsay, 4th Earl of Crawford** (\"The Tiger\"), a leading ally of the Black Douglases[1][2].\n\nThese participants are all **instances of humans (people)** — specifically, they were Scottish nobles holding peerage titles (Earls): Alexander Gordon was the 1st Earl of Huntly, and Alexander Lindsay was the 4th Earl of Crawford[1].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 135199.3, "error": ""}
