{"qid": "musique:efa92baf3840922c7dc00ba73ad729345a2b12035fa39071", "question": "Who is the federal leader of the party that Pierre-Hugues Boisvenu is a member of?", "answers": ["Andrew Scheer"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\nPierre-Hugues Boisvenu is a member of the **Conservative Party of Canada** — he was appointed to the Senate of Canada on January 29, 2010 \"under the banner of the Conservative Party of Canada,\" on the advice of Prime Minister Stephen Harper[1], and he is also listed among Senators endorsing candidates in the 2017 Conservative Party of Canada leadership election[4].\n\nRegarding the party's federal leader specifically: the retrieved documents confirm his party membership but do not contain an explicit statement naming the Conservative Party's federal leader. The only leadership-related detail in the evidence is that Stephen Harper — the Conservative Prime Minister whose government appointed Boisvenu to the Senate — was the party's leader at the time of the 2010 appointment[1]. If you need the name of the party's *current* federal leader, the knowledge base does not provide that information.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 53535.1, "error": ""}
