{"qid": "musique:0531724f1691e4d2a1e819d1e68c14edb61a1036ee25a862", "question": "Who wrote the song The Story sung by the performer of Give Up the Ghost?", "answers": ["Phil Hanseroth"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieval chain:\n\n- **Give Up the Ghost** is an album whose personnel listing includes Amy Ray on background vocals[5] — this is Brandi Carlile's 2009 album, so the performer in question is **Brandi Carlile**.\n- **\"The Story\"** — the well-known song sung by Brandi Carlile (from her 2007 album *The Story*) — was **written by Phil Hanseroth** (of the duo/band The Hanseroth twins, who also performed on her records).\n\nSo the answer is: **Phil Hanseroth** wrote \"The Story.\"\n\nOne caveat: the retrieved evidence confirms the *Give Up the Ghost* album context[5] and lists several songs titled \"The Story\"[6][7][8][9], but the snippets do not explicitly state the writer's name or Carlile's name in the returned text, so this identification relies partly on general music knowledge rather than fully verified citations.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 215796.0, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:80eb4cdc289c327a7ce40633b12e1a144052165599d2521a", "question": "Who is the president of the newly declared independent country that is part of the Commission of Truth and Friendship with the country where Sumardi was born?", "answers": ["Francisco Guterres"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n1. **Sumardi** is an Indonesian former footballer (born 26 June 1972), i.e., he was born in **Indonesia**[1].\n2. The **Commission of Truth and Friendship** was the **Indonesia–Timor Leste Commission of Truth and Friendship**, established jointly by Indonesia and East Timor (Timor-Leste)[6][7].\n\nSo the \"newly declared independent country\" involved alongside Indonesia (where Sumardi was born) is **East Timor (Timor-Leste)**, which declared its independence in 2002.\n\nAs for its president: at the time this commission was set up (2005), the president of Timor-Leste was **Xanana Gusmão**. Please note that this last detail could not be directly verified within the retrieved knowledge base excerpts due to the search limit — the KB evidence confirms the chain only up to identifying Timor-Leste as the country in question[1][6][7].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 234313.5, "error": ""}
