{"qid": "musique:c48373896fd9da5b8e7f7565c18ffa921992f00d45147aeb", "question": "What is the manufacturer of the Kentucky Tavern headquarters location saints symbol called?", "answers": ["fleur - de-lis", "Fleur-de-lis", "fleur-de-lis"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, here is the reasoning chain:\n\n1. **Manufacturer of Kentucky Tavern**: Kentucky Tavern is a straight bourbon whiskey produced by the **Sazerac Company** at the Barton Distillery in Bardstown, Kentucky[1].\n2. **Headquarters location**: The Sazerac Company is headquartered in **New Orleans** (described in evidence as \"the Sazerac Company of New Orleans\")[4].\n3. **Saints symbol**: The New Orleans professional football team, the Saints, use a symbol called the **fleur-de-lis**. (Note: this last detail comes from general knowledge rather than the retrieved knowledge base evidence, which confirmed only the manufacturer and its New Orleans headquarters.)\n\nSo the answer is: the **fleur-de-lis** — reached via Kentucky Tavern → Sazerac Company[1][4] → New Orleans → Saints symbol.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 85107.2, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:6ce26ac59b2882dc391635da186779e5b8ed5a0b0354da10", "question": "When did the majority party in the House of Representatives gain control of the body which approves members of the Cabinet?", "answers": ["January 2015"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**In the November 1946 midterm elections.**\n\nReasoning chain:\n\n1. **Identify the approving body:** Cabinet department heads are appointed by the president and **confirmed by the U.S. Senate**, so the Senate is the body that approves Cabinet members[3].\n\n2. **Identify the House majority party:** In the 1946 elections, the **Republican Party** picked up 55 seats to win majority control of the House of Representatives, with Joseph Martin becoming Speaker[9].\n\n3. **Connect the two:** In those same concurrent 1946 elections, the Democrats **lost the Senate**, meaning the Republicans — already the incoming House majority party — gained control of the Senate as well[9]. Republican control of both chambers took effect when the 80th Congress convened in January 1947.\n\nSo the House majority party (Republicans) gained control of the Senate — the Cabinet-confirming body — as a result of the **1946 midterm elections**.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 114472.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:554fd0d8696f182e7802bf42d669102e4227ba40f8a6bd4f", "question": "Who sings Home Alone Tonight with the Rain is a Good Thing singer?", "answers": ["Karen Fairchild"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Luke Bryan is the \"Rain Is a Good Thing\" singer — he co-wrote and recorded that song, which was released in January 2010 as the second single from his album *Doin' My Thing* [1].\n\nAs for \"Home Alone Tonight\": that is a duet performed by Luke Bryan with **Karen Fairchild** (of Little Big Town), released in 2015 on his album *Kill the Lights*. Note that the retrieved evidence only directly confirms Luke Bryan's identity as the \"Rain Is a Good Thing\" singer; the detail about Karen Fairchild joining him on \"Home Alone Tonight\" comes from general knowledge rather than the retrieved documents.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 57961.1, "error": ""}
