{"qid": "musique:16de423a865eb739d3ec248429096218820feb176cb1b5af", "question": "What else happened in the northern part of Erich Zakowski's birthplace in the now Russian area?", "answers": ["names were replaced by new Russian names"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, here's what I can establish:\n\nErich Zakowski was born on 25 November 1934 in **East Prussia**[2] — a region whose northern part now belongs to Russia (Kaliningrad Oblast). The related evidence notes that after the Second World War, Zakowski fled from Prussia with his mother and four siblings, initially to Dortmund, then Hamburg, before the family finally settled in Niederzissen[1].\n\nHowever, the knowledge base does not contain any further information about other events that took place specifically in the northern part of East Prussia itself. The available documents only cover Zakowski's biography and his Zakspeed racing career (founding his garage in Niederzissen in 1968, entering Formula 1 in 1985, and handing leadership to his son Peter in 1990)[1][2][4]. So, beyond his birth there and his family's post-war flight from Prussia, I don't know of any other events in that region based on the retrieved evidence.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 76908.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:f11250d4b392a30f6d22566d5167dee1464544f525c2975c", "question": "In Grown Ups, who plays the wife of the actor who produced The Chosen One?", "answers": ["Joyce Van Patten"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Joyce Van Patten** plays her.\n\nReasoning chain:\n- The film *The Chosen One* (2010) was produced by its star, **Rob Schneider**[1].\n- In *Grown Ups* (2010), Rob Schneider appears among the lead cast alongside Adam Sandler, Kevin James, Chris Rock, David Spade, Salma Hayek, Maria Bello, and Maya Rudolph[8].\n- In the film's cast listing, Schneider's character Rob Hilliard's wife **Gloria** is played by **Joyce Van Patten**[6][7].\n\nSo the wife of the actor who produced *The Chosen One* (Rob Schneider) is portrayed by Joyce Van Patten.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 97660.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:ede452592bbb410b3678e75fc6aaaeeda204fffc69034041", "question": "When did Burroughs Corporation merge to form a new corporation?", "answers": ["1986"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Burroughs Corporation merged with Sperry in **1986** to form **Unisys** — Burroughs bought Sperry for $4.8 billion, and the merger was the largest in the computer industry at the time, making Unisys the second-largest computer company with annual revenue of $10.5 billion.[1]", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 28318.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:034a82714302b4b4a869310daace9e08bb18dc7fc3a81206", "question": "When did the party that controls the House of Representatives take control of the branch who determines the rules of the US house and Senate?", "answers": ["January 2015"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- **The party that controls the House of Representatives:** The Republican Party regained control of the U.S. House in the **2010 midterm elections**, picking up a net 63 seats after having lost control to Democrats in the 2006 midterms[1].\n\n- **The branch that determines the rules of the U.S. House and Senate:** This is the United States Congress itself (the legislative branch) — under the Constitution, each chamber sets its own rules of proceedings within Congress.\n\n**Answer:** The Republican Party took control following the **November 2010 midterm elections**, formally assuming control when the new (112th) Congress convened in **January 2011**[1].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 176343.0, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:e21823470386531b4456eec33d0709c7eb82b63bc394f6fa", "question": "What series of wins did the sports team that the all time highest goal scorer in spain national team was a member or achieve in 2009?", "answers": ["continental treble"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n**Step 1 – Identify the player:** The knowledge base identifies **David Villa** as Spain's record scorer — he holds the record as top scorer in World Cup finals for Spain with 9 goals[6], and the \"Spain national football team records and statistics\" documents contain the relevant \"Most goals\" records[1].\n\n**Step 2 – The 2009 series of wins:** Unfortunately, I have to be upfront here: the retrieval limit was reached before I could pull verified evidence about the specific series of wins achieved in 2009. The retrieved snippets mention Spain's \"World Cup winners: 2010\"[7] and an all-time La Liga top scorers list[8], but none of them document a 2009 win streak tied to David Villa's team.\n\nSo, while it is widely known that Villa was Spain's all-time top scorer and that in 2009 the Spain national team went on a record-setting winning streak (including winning all ten of their 2010 World Cup qualifiers), **I cannot confirm the specific \"series of wins\" from the retrieved knowledge base evidence**, so I'd rather flag that part as unverified than guess.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 178262.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:a621901602313fe0bb3278547bfd2dc7a7eeb93905d04b78", "question": "Who followed Menucha Rochel Slonim's father?", "answers": ["Menachem Mendel Schneersohn"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Menucha Rochel Slonim's father was **Rabbi Dovber Schneuri**, the second Rebbe of the Chabad Hasidic dynasty[2]. \n\nThe person who followed (succeeded) him as Rebbe was **Menachem Mendel Schneersohn**, known as the Tzemach Tzedek, Dovber's son-in-law and nephew, who became the third Rebbe of Chabad. Note: while the knowledge base confirms Dovber Schneuri as her father[2], the succession detail is based on general historical knowledge rather than a retrieved passage, so I recommend verifying it if you need a citable source.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 90828.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:6c52099d688bcf9f3be62de4417112635370c9d72b748084", "question": "When did the country, whose co-official language was used by the director of Group Portrait with a Lady, first attend the Olympics as an independent team?", "answers": ["2016"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n1. **Director**: *Group Portrait with a Lady* (German: *Gruppenbild mit Dame*) is a 1977 German‑French drama film directed by **Aleksandar Petrović**[2].\n2. **Language/country link**: Aleksandar Petrović was a Serbian-language filmmaker (a Yugoslav/Serbian director), and Serbian is one of the co-official languages of **Bosnia and Herzegovina** (alongside Bosnian and Croatian).\n3. **Olympic debut**: Bosnia and Herzegovina first attended the Olympics as an independent team at the **1992 Summer Olympics** in Barcelona.\n\n**Answer: 1992** — the country is Bosnia and Herzegovina, whose co-official language (Serbian) was the working language of director Aleksandar Petrović[2], and it made its independent Olympic debut at the 1992 Barcelona Games.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 129279.6, "error": ""}
