{"qid": "musique:2e723619f6cb5b2fe9cffb3e419841f96bbfd79a13f07f18", "question": "Who is the father of the artist who painted Head I?", "answers": ["Nicholas Bacon", "Sir Nicholas Bacon"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Answer:** The artist who painted *Head I* is **Francis Bacon**, the Irish-born British figurative painter (the work is a 1948 oil and tempera on hardboard, the first of his six \"Heads\" series)[1][2].\n\nAs for Bacon's father, the retrieved documents confirm Bacon as the painter but did not include details about his parentage. Based on general biographical knowledge, Francis Bacon's father was **Anthony Edward Mortimer Bacon** (\"Eddy\"), an English former army captain who worked as a racehorse trainer. Please note this latter detail could not be verified against the knowledge base evidence retrieved here.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 76262.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "musique:704dd451c50a536eb50a9d580b8a57aa8203bd76d1862ef6", "question": "Where is the origin of the river Augrabies Falls is part of?", "answers": ["Thaba Putsoa"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "The Augrabies Falls are located on the **Orange River** — the river descends 122 m (400 ft) over a 26 km stretch there[1].\n\nAs for its origin: the Orange River **rises in the Drakensberg mountains along the border between South Africa and Lesotho**, about 193 km (120 mi) west of the Indian Ocean, at an altitude of over 3,000 m (9,800 ft)[6]. It then flows westwards through South Africa to the Atlantic Ocean[8].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 101102.0, "error": ""}
