{"qid": "musique:bfcfaa4a93f27ba34411adfc4a326e54fa373314b0ba15ab", "question": "Who is the son of the Italian navigator who explored the eastern coast of the continent Ulises Solís' birthplace is located in for England?", "answers": ["Sebastian Cabot"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Sebastian Cabot.**\n\nReasoning chain from the retrieved evidence:\n\n1. **Ulises Solís' continent:** José Ulises Solís Pérez is a Mexican former professional boxer who held the IBF junior flyweight title twice[6]. Since his birthplace is in Mexico, the continent in question is **North America**.\n\n2. **The navigator:** The Italian navigator who explored the eastern coast of North America sailing for England was **John Cabot**, a 15th-century Italian explorer recognized for his 1497 voyage discovering Newfoundland[2].\n\n3. **His son:** John Cabot's son was **Sebastian Cabot**, who also became an explorer, contributing to the mapping and exploration of parts of North and South America[2], and later served King Henry VIII as a cartographer before accompanying expeditions to Spain[4].\n\nSo the answer is **Sebastian Cabot**.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 74097.1, "error": ""}
