{"qid": "2wikimqa:be97290f663a83ba27007dd262ca2a6072c9156f775a24ad", "question": "Where does the director of film Wine Of Morning work at?", "answers": ["Bob Jones University"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The 1955 film *Wine of Morning* was directed by **Katherine Stenholm**[4]. Based on the retrieved evidence, her work is associated with **Unusual Films** — the film production company of Bob Jones University — as *Wine of Morning* is featured on the Unusual Films website (unusualfilms.com)[1] and the film is based on a novel by Bob Jones Jr.[3]\n\nSo, the director of *Wine of Morning*, Katherine Stenholm, works at Unusual Films (Bob Jones University).", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 70013.5, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:c8fd8db4d295aef41a9434299a8eeffb9af5e2bbcde4f13a", "question": "Who is Helmichis's father-in-law?", "answers": ["Cunimund"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the knowledge base: Helmichis was a Lombard noble who assassinated King Alboin in 572 and then married Alboin's queen, Rosamund [5]. Through that marriage, his father-in-law was **Cunimund**, king of the Gepids — Rosamund's father.\n\nNote: the retrieved evidence directly confirms the marriage to Rosamund [5], while the identification of Cunimund as her father comes from the standard historical accounts of Rosamund's lineage; the search snippets did not include that explicit sentence, so please treat that final link with slight caution.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 116304.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:90f7f51f0c27f041e730cf8893f79f3f40fcb0aab1820a4d", "question": "Who is Renaud Ii, Count Of Soissons's uncle?", "answers": ["Guy II, Count of Soissons"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, I can't identify an uncle by name for Renaud II, Count of Soissons. What the records do show is:\n\n- Renaud II, Count of Soissons is directly associated with **Adelaide, Countess of Soissons**, who was his mother (she held the county before him)[1]\n- Adelaide was herself the daughter of **Renaud I, Count of Soissons**[4]\n\nThat makes Renaud I, Count of Soissons his **maternal grandfather** rather than his uncle. The retrieved documents do not explicitly name anyone as Renaud II's uncle, so I cannot confirm a specific uncle from this knowledge base.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "entity_relation_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 128114.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:b3845fcad97309850a76e3720cd829a45d2bb12ee29a9cfb", "question": "Where was the director of film Kanneshwara Rama born?", "answers": ["Mysore"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- The 1977 Kannada political film *Kanneshwara Rama* was directed by **M. S. Sathyu**[3].\n- Regarding his origins, the knowledge base states that Sathyu was born into a Kannada Brahmin family and **grew up in Mysore**, pursuing higher education at Mysore and later Bangalore[6].\n\nSo, the director of *Kanneshwara Rama*, M. S. Sathyu, was from **Mysore** (Karnataka, India) — the knowledge base confirms he was born into a Kannada Brahmin family and raised/educated in Mysore[6].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "entity_relation_lookup"], "latency_ms": 65707.5, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:5844352bd3fe5898756970abec3099ec694be6ad15c498db", "question": "Which film came out earlier, Indradhanura Chhai or The Death Of Black King?", "answers": ["The Death Of Black King"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**The Death of Black King** came out earlier. It is a Czechoslovak film released in **1971**, starring Vlastimil Brodský, Jaroslav Marvan, Josef Vinklář, and others[6]. By comparison, *Indradhanura Chhai* (an Indian/Oriya film directed by Anjana Chowdhury) was released much later, in 1993, so the 1971 Czechoslovak film predates it by over two decades.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 77942.2, "error": ""}
