{"qid": "2wikimqa:fac1e789f954097c329b2709c591f0b35841438b14d08784", "question": "Which country Keōpūolani's husband is from?", "answers": ["Kingdom of Hawaii"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Keōpūolani's husband was **King Kamehameha I** — she was his highest-ranking wife and queen consort of Hawaiʻi[1]. He was from **Hawaii**, ruling as Aliʻi nui (king) of Hawaii Island and later of the unified Hawaiian Islands[6][8].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 87822.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:1d38c4b905f131417ce218eb86f68305a10160f9757cbeca", "question": "Which film came out first, The Pyrammmid or Revolt Of The Praetorians?", "answers": ["Revolt Of The Praetorians"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Revolt of the Praetorians** came out first. It was released in **1964** — La Rivolta dei Pretoriani is a sword-and-sandal film directed by Alfonso Brescia starring Richard Harrison[8]. By contrast, *The Pyramid* is a much more recent film (released in 2014), so the 1964 Italian historical drama predates it by five decades.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 141816.3, "error": ""}
