{"qid": "2wikimqa:0c4dd15b43d1061d372c11946aa71630926e2570f333f538", "question": "Who lived longer, Charles Wheatstone or Jean-Claude Lauzon?", "answers": ["Charles Wheatstone"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Charles Wheatstone lived longer.**\n\nBased on the retrieved evidence:\n- **Charles Wheatstone** was born on 6 February 1802 and died on 19 October 1875, at the age of **73**[5][3].\n- No knowledge base evidence was retrieved for **Jean-Claude Lauzon**, so his lifespan could not be verified here. From general knowledge, the Canadian filmmaker Jean-Claude Lauzon (1953–1997) died in a plane crash at about age 44 — far younger than Wheatstone.\n\nSo even without KB verification for Lauzon, Wheatstone (73 years) clearly outlived him.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 79872.1, "error": ""}
