{"qid": "2wikimqa:cdf0b77af7d55cc9a3424613604e8dbabe7a01e4869ad502", "question": "Where did Mary Of Woodstock's mother die?", "answers": ["Harby"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Mary of Woodstock's mother was **Eleanor of Castile**, as Mary was \"the seventh named daughter of Edward I of England and Eleanor of Castile\" [4].\n\nHowever, the retrieved evidence does not explicitly state where Eleanor of Castile died. From general historical knowledge, Eleanor of Castile died on 28 November 1290 at **Harby, Nottinghamshire** (in the house of a man named Richard de Weston), after which her body was taken to London for burial at Westminster Abbey — commemorated by the famous Eleanor Crosses erected along the funeral procession route.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 62636.7, "error": ""}
